---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout
  title="Event pipeline for B2B | Kadanco"
  description="Events scored by ICP overlap, pre-event ABM with calendar holds, hosted dinners and roundtables, same-day enrichment and CRM sync, and an ROI report inside 30 days. Run end to end by two operators."
>
  <main id="top">

    <!-- ===================== HERO ===================== -->
    <section class="hero" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow">Use case &middot; Event pipeline</span>
        <h1>Most event budgets buy a booth.<br><span class="hl">Yours should buy meetings.</span></h1>
        <p class="lead">Turning up is not a strategy. We pick events on the numbers, warm the room for four weeks before anyone travels, book meetings into a held calendar, and follow up the same day. Then we hand you a report your CFO can read.</p>
        <div class="hero-cta">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Get a free audit</button>
          <p class="hero-cta-note">Tell us which events you're committed to. We'll tell you what they're worth.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHY EVENTS DON'T PAY ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-paper" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow dark">Why events don't pay</span>
        <h2>The spend is committed. <span class="hl-indigo">The pipeline is not.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>The event was picked on feel</h3>
            <p>Chosen because a competitor sponsors it or someone went last year, not because your buyers are actually in the room.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Nobody knew you were coming</h3>
            <p>The team lands with an empty calendar and hopes for traffic, so the best conversations happen by accident.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>The follow-up goes cold</h3>
            <p>Badges sit in a spreadsheet for two weeks. By the time anyone reaches out, the room has forgotten the conversation.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== THE RUNWAY ===================== -->
    <section class="section" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow indigo">The runway</span>
        <h2>The work happens <span class="hl-indigo">before and after the event.</span></h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px;max-width:740px">
          The two days on the floor are the smallest part. This is the motion around them.
        </p>
        <div style="max-width:1040px;margin:44px auto 0">
          <svg viewBox="0 0 1200 300" data-anim="diagram" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" style="width:100%;height:auto;display:block" role="img" aria-label="An event runway: six weeks out we score the events, four weeks out ABM starts, one week out meetings are booked into held calendars, on the day we host dinners and roundtables, and within 30 days follow-up is done and the ROI report is delivered.">
            <path d="M120 130 L 1080 130" stroke="#B2B1FF" stroke-width="3" stroke-linecap="round"/>

            <g font-family="Fira Sans" text-anchor="middle">
              <!-- 1 -->
              <circle cx="120" cy="130" r="12" fill="#3B38DF"/>
              <text x="120" y="92" font-size="13" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#5A5A72">6 WEEKS OUT</text>
              <text x="120" y="180" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#201E1F">Score the events</text>
              <text x="120" y="202" font-size="14" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72">ICP overlap, persona density</text>
              <!-- 2 -->
              <circle cx="360" cy="130" r="12" fill="#3B38DF"/>
              <text x="360" y="92" font-size="13" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#5A5A72">4 WEEKS OUT</text>
              <text x="360" y="180" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#201E1F">ABM starts</text>
              <text x="360" y="202" font-size="14" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72">LinkedIn and Meta to the list</text>
              <!-- 3 -->
              <circle cx="600" cy="130" r="12" fill="#3B38DF"/>
              <text x="600" y="92" font-size="13" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#5A5A72">1 WEEK OUT</text>
              <text x="600" y="180" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#201E1F">Calendar holds</text>
              <text x="600" y="202" font-size="14" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72">meetings booked before travel</text>
              <!-- 4 -->
              <circle cx="840" cy="130" r="12" fill="#3B38DF"/>
              <text x="840" y="92" font-size="13" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#5A5A72">EVENT DAY</text>
              <text x="840" y="180" font-size="17" font-weight="600" fill="#201E1F">Dinners and roundtables</text>
              <text x="840" y="202" font-size="14" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72">where deals actually move</text>
              <!-- 5 -->
              <circle cx="1080" cy="130" r="16" fill="#DAFF02"/>
              <text x="1080" y="92" font-size="13" font-weight="600" letter-spacing="1.2" fill="#3B38DF">WITHIN 30 DAYS</text>
              <text x="1080" y="180" font-size="17" font-weight="700" fill="#201E1F">Follow-up and ROI</text>
              <text x="1080" y="202" font-size="14" font-weight="500" fill="#5A5A72">same-day sync, then the report</text>
            </g>
          </svg>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHAT WE RUN ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-deep" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">What we run</span>
        <h2>The whole motion, <span class="hl">not the booth.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-2" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Events scored, not guessed</h3>
            <p>Every event on your list scored by ICP overlap and persona density, so the budget goes where your buyers actually are and the rest gets cut.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>ABM from four weeks out</h3>
            <p>LinkedIn and Meta aimed at the attendee list, with calendar holds going out early, so the room recognises you before anyone walks in.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Dinners and roundtables</h3>
            <p>Hosted formats where real conversations happen, organised end to end: venue, invitations, the guest list and the run of show.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Same-day follow-up</h3>
            <p>Enrichment, CRM sync and sequenced follow-up on the day, while the conversation is still fresh, with every meeting tagged.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== WHAT YOU OWN ===================== -->
    <section class="section band-paper" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow dark">What you own</span>
        <h2>A calendar, <span class="hl-indigo">and a number you can defend.</span></h2>
        <div class="grid cols-3" style="margin-top:48px;text-align:left">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>A room that knows you</h3>
            <p>Attendees who have seen you for four weeks before the event, so the first conversation starts warm.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Meetings, not badge scans</h3>
            <p>A held calendar your team walks into, instead of a stack of leads nobody can rank afterwards.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>A report for the CFO</h3>
            <p>Within 30 days, every meeting tagged and traced to pipeline, so next year's event budget is a decision, not an argument.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== ONE USE CASE NOTE ===================== -->
    <section class="section center" data-theme="light">
      <div class="container">
        <p class="lead" style="max-width:720px;margin:0 auto">
          Event pipeline is one of the ways teams put Kadanco to work. It is one use case, not the whole offer. The same two operators run the full marketing function for B2B companies. <a class="hl-indigo" href="/">See how the full function works</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ===================== FINAL CTA ===================== -->
    <section class="section cta-band center" data-theme="dark">
      <div class="container">
        <span class="eyebrow peri">Lets Talk</span>
        <h2>Which events are <span class="hl">already booked?</span></h2>
        <p class="lead" style="margin-top:20px">Send us the list. We'll score them, tell you which ones are worth the spend, then run the motion around them.</p>
        <div class="cta-actions">
          <button class="btn btn-primary btn-lg" data-open-modal>Get a free audit</button>
        </div>
        <p class="cta-note">Free, no obligation. We'll get back to you quickly.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

  </main>
</Layout>
